Author:     Viche Executive <executive@viche.local>
AuthorDate: Sun Nov 8 10:05:10 2026 +0000
Commit:     Viche Executive <executive@viche.local>
CommitDate: Sun Nov 8 10:05:10 2026 +0000

    appointments+branch-liveness: bounded re-probe for transient 'unknown'
    
    Companion to 9be9652, which fixes only executive-cycle.sh. In the real call path
    executive-cycle.sh calls 'appointments.sh ensure executive' BEFORE its own status
    case, so a single transient 'unknown' sample from Antonina still exits 1 there
    first; the branch supervisor's readiness probe also writes 'unhealthy' from one
    sample. Verified: the new smoke fails on 9be9652 alone ('unknown status unknown',
    no dispatch).
    
    This commit adds the same bounded (3x1s) re-probe to the appointments.sh mutation
    path and to both branch-liveness.sh probes. Persistent unknown still fails closed
    - mutations need a positively identified terminal state, and the branch stays
    unhealthy - but now reports the agent, state and re-probe count instead of an
    anonymous failure. No health is inferred from an unresolved sample.
    
    tests/unknown-status-transient-smoke.sh fails on origin/main and on 9be9652
    alone, and passes here: a one-sample unknown still dispatches and yields
    readiness 'ready'; a persistent unknown dispatches nothing and exits 1.

diff --git a/government/appointments.sh b/government/appointments.sh
index c6b85f5f..34a0fcf1 100644
--- a/government/appointments.sh
+++ b/government/appointments.sh
@@ -69,6 +69,19 @@ if [ -n "$old" ]; then
     exit 1
   fi
   status=$(printf '%s\n' "$meta" | jq -er '.state') || exit 1
+  # One "unknown" sample is a transient runtime observation, not a terminal
+  # state: re-probe a bounded number of times before deciding. A persistent
+  # unknown still fails closed for mutations below.
+  probe=0
+  while [ "$status" = unknown ] && [ "$probe" -lt 3 ]; do
+    probe=$((probe + 1))
+    sleep 1
+    if meta=$(antonina agent status --id "$old" --json 2>/dev/null); then
+      status=$(printf '%s\n' "$meta" | jq -er '.state' 2>/dev/null) || status=unknown
+    else
+      status=unknown
+    fi
+  done
   case "$status" in
     running|idle|clearexit) live=true;;
     failed|stopped|killed) :;;
@@ -79,7 +92,7 @@ if [ -n "$old" ]; then
       # sample breaks every caller (sitting, liveness, oversight). Mutations
       # still require a positively identified terminal state.
       if [ "$action" = resolve ]; then live=unknown
-      else echo "unknown status $status" >&2; exit 1
+      else echo "Viche: appointed agent $old still reports '$status' after $probe re-probe(s); refuse $action until a terminal state is proven" >&2; exit 1
       fi;;
   esac
 fi
